On 2002-02-11 18:51, Healy wrote:
Well I guess this will be my final post here...dissapointing the way things went down here...

First off I want to say I had nothing to do with whatever had happened...those who actually know me know its the truth those who don't I don't care anyway.  

I have been thinking about leaving as the guild has really outgrown me...recent events have cemented that feeling.  Couldn't believe that when I logged on I hear Effix saying that I was involved in the incident...why didnt you ask me first?  That was really upsetting...then the next day I got no less than 5 nasty tells saying that I was a traitor etc etc...that's bullshit guys...I would have thought after spending 3+ years in this guild I would be given the common courtesy of being asked if I was involved or if I had prior knowledge of it...

I can't believe what this guild has become...I won't judge because thats what alot of ppl wanted the guild to become so its none of my business...However, listen to yourselves...I agree that what Arachnis did was hurtful, but was it really that harmful?  Think about it from his point of view...the hours he put into the site for a game that he no longer played but simply because he wanted to remain a part of the guild...What did we do?  We all complained about parts not being added or the site not being updated fast enough...On the numerous occasions he asked for help we ignored him...and we call him a traitor, think about that, that must not have been an easy decision for him.  I don't really know what happened b/w charoth/effix/arachnis/valandra and I don't really care but from what I am seeing now I am beginning to see the light.  I cared deeply about this guild, I have been through the start of a marriage, 2 kids, graduation from University and the start of a career all while belonging to this collective.  I have considered many of you friends, even though we may have had some disagreements in the past.  But look at what we have become or are in the process of becoming...wonder why so many people are leaving?  why a large percentage of the server dislikes our guildtag?  Are we right in all instances?  
I invite us all to post here, I would love to hear Arachnis' feelings on the matter as well as some of you other members old and new...

As I begin to shine whilst stepping back into the light I speak softly yet clearly, "Fare Thee Well Oblivion, It has been a great journey and one that I shall never regret..."

For those of you that will remain friends, and even those that won't, send me a tell in game, group with me, shout to me, or sell me some loot, just don't ignore me...

Healy HealBringer  member of the Order 
Sept. 1998-Feb.11 2002

